<p>The University of Leipzig is launching a new, tuition-free English-language Master of Arts program in philosophy.<span id="more-56817"></span></p>
<p><img decoding="async" class=" wp-image-56818 aligncenter" src="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/university-leipzig.jpg" alt="" width="861" height="500" srcset="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/university-leipzig.jpg 1200w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/university-leipzig-300x174.jpg 300w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/university-leipzig-1024x595.jpg 1024w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/university-leipzig-768x446.jpg 768w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/university-leipzig-400x232.jpg 400w" sizes="(max-width: 861px) 100vw, 861px" /></p>
<p>Professor Kristina Musholt writes that it is a two-year program &#8220;with a diverse range of courses that create the conditions for acquiring in-depth skills in academic work, placing particular emphasis on guiding and promoting independent philosophical research.&#8221;</p>
<p>The program, which is accepting applications now, will start in the winter term of 2026-27, which runs October through March.</p>
<p>You can learn more about the program at the University of Leipzig Institute for Philosophy <a href="https://www.sozphil.uni-leipzig.de/en/institute-of-philosophy/about-the-institute" target="_blank" rel="noopener">website</a>, with instructions about applying <a href="https://www.sozphil.uni-leipzig.de/institut-fuer-philosophie/studium-1/studiengaenge#c351642" target="_blank" rel="noopener">here</a>. Advice for international students is <a href="https://www.uni-leipzig.de/en/international/contact-and-advice" target="_blank" rel="noopener">here</a>.</p><p>The post <a href="https://dailynous.com/2026/03/09/new-free-ma-program-in-philosophy/">New: Free MA Program in Philosophy</a> first appeared on <a href="https://dailynous.com">Daily Nous</a>.</p>